    "body": "I can see that reasoning, but, (a) requiring waiting on cross-process messages for what would otherwise be very simple navigations is not great; and (b) beforeunload is generally bad, so the less of it we fire, the better IMO. If it's already not fired in 2/3 browsers in these cases, I'm inclined to spec that behavior.\r\n\r\nThis is pending some test results for the non-javascript: cases, though.",
